<th id="S5.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Accuracy (%)</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mask-alive</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Deployable</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cycles</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">No-minimize baseline</span></th>
<td id="S5.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.99\pm 0.84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">95.99</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.84</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.99\pm 0.84</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{,}354\pm 196" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3,354</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">196</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{,}354\pm 196</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18{,}126\pm 2{,}824" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">18,126</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2,824</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18{,}126\pm 2{,}824</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.2\pm 1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4.2</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.2\pm 1.8</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S5.T1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Squeeze-Release</span></th>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="97.03\pm 0.56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">97.03</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.56</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">97.03\pm 0.56</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{,}878\pm 1{,}584" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4,878</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1,584</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{,}878\pm 1{,}584</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{,}878\pm 1{,}584" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4,878</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1,584</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{,}878\pm 1{,}584</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11.6\pm 3.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">11.6</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.6\pm 3.7</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>FC on MNIST: 5-seed mean <math id="S5.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> standard deviation.
<em id="S5.T1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mask-alive</em> is the count of non-zero entries in the persisted pruning mask at the end of the last successful cycle; <em id="S5.T1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Deployable</em> is the parameter count of the dense network after the structural rewrite of <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Exact minimization (squeeze): dead-incoming and dead-outgoing units ‣ 3 Method ‣ Squeeze-Release: Iterative Pruning with Exact Structural Minimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
For Squeeze-Release these two values coincide by construction as models use all available capacity.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>ConvNeXt-Tiny on CIFAR-10</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.T2" title="In 5.2 ConvNeXt-Tiny on CIFAR-10 ‣ 5 Results ‣ Squeeze-Release: Iterative Pruning with Exact Structural Minimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports 5-seed mean and standard deviation for the No-minimize baseline and Squeeze-Release in Modes A and AB on the <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27{,}827{,}818" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>27,827,818</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27{,}827{,}818</annotation></semantics></math>-parameter ConvNeXt-Tiny model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the Mode AB structural rewrite once, post hoc, to the No-minimize baseline reduces the deployable size to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.0</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters on average, a <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.78\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.78</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.78\times</annotation></semantics></math> reduction from the full model with no training-loop change.
Squeeze-Release Mode AB pushes this to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.88" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.88</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.88</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> smaller than the post-hoc-minimized baseline and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="14.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>14.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14.8\times</annotation></semantics></math> smaller than the full pre-trained model, at <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90.27\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>90.27</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90.27\%</annotation></semantics></math> test accuracy versus <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90.81\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>90.81</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90.81\%</annotation></semantics></math> for the baseline.
Mode A is less aggressive on size (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.45</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.45</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4.1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.1\times</annotation></semantics></math> smaller than the baseline or <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="11.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.4\times</annotation></semantics></math> smaller than the full pre-trained model) and reaches <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="91.14\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>91.14</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">91.14\%</annotation></semantics></math> test accuracy.
No accuracy difference relative to the baseline is statistically significant under Welch’s t-test with Bonferroni correction (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{adj}=0.52" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.52</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{adj}=0.52</annotation></semantics></math> for Mode A, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.11</annotation></semantics></math> for Mode AB) or raw Welch’s t-test (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.26</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.26</annotation></semantics></math> for Mode A, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.055" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.055</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.055</annotation></semantics></math> for Mode AB).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The contribution of Stage B is directly visible from the difference between Mode A and Mode AB.
Enabling residual-stream reduction via <em id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CompensatedLayerNorm</em> (<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 CompensatedLayerNorm: exact channel reduction across LayerNorm ‣ 3 Method ‣ Squeeze-Release: Iterative Pruning with Exact Structural Minimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) shrinks the deployable model by an additional <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> on top of Stage A, providing empirical justification for the LayerNorm rewrite.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A per-call unit test confirms the rewrite stays exact throughout: across all ConvNeXt minimization calls the smaller dense network reproduces the original forward function to within floating-point precision, with maximum absolute logit difference <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.06{\times}10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.06</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.06{\times}10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> across all experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The mask-vs-deployable gap behaves qualitatively as on FC but is wider.
The No-minimize baseline ends with <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="884" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>884</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">884</annotation></semantics></math>k non-zero mask entries on average while the deployable dense network has <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.0</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters: the deployable size is <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="11.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> larger than the mask-alive count, roughly twice the gap observed on FC.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We have capped the number of cycles to 100 to save computational resources.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
